<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Catalog Doc

`CATALOG_DOC_URI = bagUri("catalog")` names the catalog document (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-uris.ts`). Its `tiddlers` map holds registry records whose `text` fields carry Automerge document URLs. The genesis row gives the catalog `readPolicy: "public"` and `writePolicy: "private"` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/genesis-doc.ts`).

Keep the catalog small: registry pointers belong here; tiddler bodies and corpus content belong in their own documents. The content-plane law stands at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/automerge-tiga#/tiga-law`>>.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/entries`>>

!! Registry Entries

`catalogCorpusEntryUri(slug)` builds a key under `CATALOG_CORPUS_PREFIX`, `${CATALOG_DOC_URI}/corpus/`; its record's `text` carries the corpus child-doc URL (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-uris.ts`). `corpusLarUri(slug)` names that corpus bag (`lar-uris.ts`).

`loadCatalogCorpora` scans catalog tiddler keys with that prefix, reads each record's `text` as a doc URL, resolves the handle, and adds the corpus as a read-only composite layer. A declared mesh scale routes through `resolveBootDoc`; an entry without that scale uses the vessel's local handle factory (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/load-corpora.ts`). Both vessel composers supply this loader (`packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts`; `packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts`).

Wiki leaves use `wikiBagUri(slug) = bagUri(slug)` as catalog keys (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts`). The catalog accessor reads a bag key's record `text` to find its URL, then resolves its document; a request for `CATALOG_DOC_URI` returns the catalog handle directly (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/catalog-accessor.ts`). Wiki activation also reads the `wikiBagUri(slug)` record and requires an `automerge:` URL (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/vessel-residency-wiring.ts`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/law`>>

!! Catalog Law

* The catalog reads public and writes private (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/genesis-doc.ts`).
* Keep the catalog small: no tiddler text bodies or full corpus content.
* An Automerge URL locates bytes; it never authorizes access (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/automerge-tiga#/tiga-law`>>).

<<~/ahu>>

